==English==

===Etymology===
{{prefix|en|ecto|plasm}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɛktəˌplæzəm/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}
{{wikipedia}}

# {{lb|en|parapsychology}} A [[visible]] [[substance]] believed to [[emanate]] from the body of a [[spiritualistic]] [[medium]] during [[communication]] with the [[dead]].
#* {{RQ:Lowry Under the Volcano|page=137|passage=He saw again clearly enough{{...|—as Dr. Vigil, recognizing him with a smile, closed his paper and hastened toward him—}}the doctor’s consulting room in the Avenida de la Revolución, visited for some drunken reason in the early hours of the morning, macabre with its pictures of ancient Spanish surgeons, their goat faces rising queerly from ruffs resembling '''ectoplasm''', roaring with laughter as they performed inquisitorial operations; {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2021|author=[[w:Jenni Fagan|Jenni Fagan]]|title=Luckenbooth|publisher=William Heinemann|page=131|passage=Watching as the woman lifted her skirts and flung out '''ectoplasm''', expelled it into a bowl, then brandished it around at her audience wildly.}}
# {{lb|en|parapsychology}} An [[immaterial]] or [[ethereal]] substance, especially the [[transparent]] [[corporeal]] presence of a spirit or [[ghost]].
#* {{RQ:Doyle Land of Mist|passage=Then came some hollow groanings from inside the cabinet. The Spiritualists sat up expectantly. "That's '''ectoplasm'''," said Ogilvy. "It always causes pain on emission."}}
# {{lb|en|cytology}} The outer [[granule]]-free layer of [[cytoplasm]].

